{"id":332,"flavor":[{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"If a traveler is going through a desert in the thick of night, Cacturne will follow in a ragtag group. The Pokémon are biding their time, waiting for the traveler to tire and become incapable of moving."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"During the daytime, Cacturne remains unmoving so that it does not lose any moisture to the harsh desert sun. This Pokémon becomes active at night when the temperature drops."},{"games":["Y","SoulSilver","HeartGold"],"text":"Packs of them follow travelers through the desert until the travelers can no longer move."},{"games":["X","White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"It becomes active at night, seeking prey that is exhausted from the day’s desert heat."},{"games":["LeafGreen","FireRed"],"text":"It lives in deserts. It becomes active at night when it hunts for prey exhausted from the desert’s heat."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"After spending thousands of years in harsh deserts, its blood transformed into the same substances as sand. It is nocturnal, so it hunts at night."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Sand Veil","hidden":false,"description":"Boosts the Pokémon's evasiveness in a sandstorm."},{"name":"Water Absorb","hidden":true,"description":"If hit by a Water-type move, the Pokémon has its HP restored instead of taking damage."}],"eggGroups":["Grass","Human-Like"],"genderRate":4,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":35,"growthRate":"medium slow","habitat":"rough terrain","color":"Green","shape":"Humanoid","evolution":{"id":331,"name":"Cacnea","condition":null,"children":[{"id":332,"name":"Cacturne","condition":"Lv. 32","children":[]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[0,596],[1,40],[1,43],[1,71],[1,74],[1,194],[10,73],[13,28],[16,331],[19,681],[22,275],[26,371],[30,191],[35,389],[38,42],[44,412],[49,178],[54,201]],"machine":[34,280,523,331,174,399,91,409,227,283,203,412,263,374,411,264,492,202,416,447,803,580,270,63,282,808